#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "This documentation describes &kde;'s control center."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "kcontrol"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kcontrolcenter; (from now on referred to simply as <quote>the control "
"center</quote>) provides you with a centralized and convenient way to "
"configure all of your &kde; settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The control center is made up of multiple modules. Each module is a separate "
"application, but the control center organizes all of these programs into a "
"convenient location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each control center module can be executed individually"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See section entitled <link linkend=\"control-center-run-indiv\">Running "
"individual control center modules</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The control center groups the configuration modules into categories, so they "
"are easy to locate. Within each category, the control center shows all the "
"modules in a list, so it is easier to find the right configuration module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the &kcontrolcenter;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This next section details the use of the control center itself. For "
"information on individual modules, please see <link linkend=\"module"
"\">Control Center Modules</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting the &kcontrol;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kcontrolcenter; can be started in 3 ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>K Button</guimenu><guimenuitem>Control "
"Center</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the &kde; Panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box. Type <userinput><command>kcontrol</"
"command></userinput>, and click <guibutton>Run</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can type <command>kcontrol &amp;</command> at any command prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "All three of these methods are equivalent, and produce the same result."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kcontrolcenter; Screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start the control center, you are presented with a window, which "
"can be divided into 3 functional parts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Screenshot</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Screenshot</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Control Center Screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Across the top is a menubar. The menubar will provide you with quick access "
"to most of &kcontrolcenter;'s features. The menus are detailed in <link "
"linkend=\"control-center-menus\">The &kde; Control Center Menus</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Along the left hand side, is a icon tree. Here you can choose which module "
"to configure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main panel shows you some system information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this example, we are running &kde; 3.4.0, we started &kcontrolcenter; as "
"user <systemitem class=\"username\">newkde</systemitem>, the computer is "
"named <systemitem class=\"systemname\">turtle</systemitem>, it is a &Linux; "
"system running the 2.6 kernel, on a i686 processor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kcontrolcenter; Menus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This next section gives you a brief description of what each menu item does."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu has a single entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Closes the control center."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "These options determine how the module selection looks and behaves."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Mode</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Determines whether to use <guimenuitem>Tree</guimenuitem> view, or "
"<guimenuitem>Icon</guimenuitem> view for your modules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <guimenuitem>Tree</guimenuitem> view, each submenu appears as an "
"indented list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <guimenuitem>Icon</guimenuitem> view, when you click on a category, the "
"categories disappear and are replaced with the module list. You then use the "
"<guiicon>Back</guiicon> button to return to the categories."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Icon size</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this option, you can choose <guimenuitem>Small</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Medium</guimenuitem>, or <guimenuitem>Large</guimenuitem> icons "
"to select your modules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This menu item only controls the icon size if you are in <guimenuitem>Icon "
"View</guimenuitem>. If you choose <guimenuitem>Tree View</guimenuitem>, the "
"<guimenuitem>Small</guimenuitem> icon size will be used, no matter what size "
"was previously selected in <guimenuitem>Icon View</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu has a single entry, "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. From here you can map keyboard shortcuts to the "
"other menu options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Help</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: sect2
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "&help.menu.documentation;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exiting The &kde; Control Center"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can exit the control center one of three ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menu bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> on the "
"keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guiicon>Close</guiicon> button on the frame surrounding the "
"control center."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "Running Individual Modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can run individual modules without running kcontrol using the command "
"<command>kcmshell4</command> from &konsole;. Type <userinput> "
"<command>kcmshell4</command><option> --list</option></userinput> to see a "
"list of the available &kcontrolcenter; modules. You can also access "
"individual &kcontrolcenter; modules through adding the "
"<guilabel>Preferences</guilabel> button to either &kicker; or the &kmenu; "
"through their respective configuration dialogs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kcontrolcenter; Modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to make it as easy as possible, the &kcontrolcenter; has organized "
"similar options into groups. Each group is called a module. When you click "
"on the name of a module in the left window, you will be presented with the "
"options of the module on the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each module will have some or all of the following buttons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr "Ajuda"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button will give you help specific to the current module. The button "
"will show you a short summary help page in the left window. At the bottom of "
"that window, you can click on a link to get more detailed help."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defaults"
msgstr "Valors per defaut"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button will restore this module to its default values. You must click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save the options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply"
msgstr "Aplicar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking this button will save all changes to &kde;. If you have changed "
"anything, clicking <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> will cause the changes to "
"take effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reset"
msgstr "Reinicializar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button will <quote>Reset</quote> the module to the previous settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must save the options of the current module using <guibutton>Apply</"
"guibutton> before you can change to a different module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you try to change without saving your options, you will be asked if you "
"want to save your changes, or discard them."
msgstr ""

